UID:creative-nz-international-engagement-fund-2026-27-round-1@artificialnou
 veau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T210426Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative New Zealand: International Engagement Fund 2026/
 27 (Round 1)
DESCRIPTION:Creative New Zealand's International Engagement Fund pays for N
 ew Zealand artists\, practitioners and arts organisations to take part in 
 international opportunities: touring\, showcasing\, presenting\, exhibitin
 g\, collaborating and being seen by overseas presenters. Eligible costs ar
 e international travel and freight\, marketing and promotion\, and the tra
 vel\, accommodation and hosting costs of getting international presenters 
 in front of New Zealand work off-shore. Up to NZ$25\,000 per application. 
 ELIGIBILITY: New Zealand citizens or permanent residents\, and New Zealand
 -based arts organisations and groups\, who have a current international st
 rategy and are internationally ready. International presenters and cultura
 l agencies can also apply for a confirmed opportunity involving New Zealan
 d artists\, and for requests over NZ$5\,000 must contribute towards the co
 sts themselves. For any request over NZ$5\,000 the applicant must already 
 hold an offer or invitation to take part\; smaller requests are looser. PR
 OCESS: submit an expression of interest first (applicant details\, an elig
 ibility check and declaration\, and an outline of the international opport
 unity)\, then complete a full application if invited. Two rounds in 2026/2
 7\, both opened 17 August 2026: Round 1 closes 1.00pm NZ time on 10 Septem
 ber 2026 with results by 5 November 2026\, Round 2 closes 1.00pm NZ time o
 n 3 December 2026 with results by 28 January 2027. Requests up to NZ$5\,00
 0 may be decided sooner. Apply through the Creative New Zealand portal. No
  application fee.\n\nOrganisation: Creative New Zealand (Arts Council of N
 ew Zealand Toi Aotearoa)\nLocation: Aotearoa New Zealand\, for activity th
 at takes place internationally. Applicants must be New Zealand citizens or
  permanent residents\, or New Zealand-based arts organisations and groups.
  International presenters and cultural agencies bringing New Zealand artis
 ts or work to their own country may also apply.\nAward: Up to NZ$25\,000 p
 er application. Covers international travel and freight\, marketing and pr
 omotion\, and the travel\, accommodation and hosting costs of bringing int
 ernational presenters to see New Zealand work off-shore. No application fe
 e.\nDuration: Project-based\; funds one specific international opportunity
 .\n\nMore: https://creativenz.govt.nz/funding-and-support/all-opportunitie
 s/international-engagement-fund?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
URL:https://creativenz.govt.nz/funding-and-support/all-opportunities/intern
 ational-engagement-fund?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
LOCATION:Aotearoa New Zealand\, for activity that takes place international
 ly. Applicants must be New Zealand citizens or permanent residents\, or Ne
 w Zealand-based arts organisations and groups. International presenters an
 d cultural agencies bringing New Zealand artists or work to their own coun
 try may also apply.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:creative-nz-creative-impact-fund-2026-round-2@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260904T210426Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260917
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260918
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative New Zealand: Creative Impact Fund 2026 (Round 2)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Impact Fund is Creative New Zealand's project fund
  for artists and practitioners making and presenting work with real reach:
  creating\, developing\, presenting\, touring or publishing across any art
 form. Two funding tiers\, up to NZ$50\,000 and between NZ$50\,000 and NZ$1
 25\,000\, with the larger tier held to a higher bar on impact and delivery
 . ELIGIBILITY: artists and practitioners who are New Zealand citizens or p
 ermanent residents\, applying as individuals or as a group of collaborator
 s. Arts organisations and groups cannot apply to this fund\; they are serv
 ed by the separate organisations funds. Sole traders and people who operat
 e through a company can still apply as individuals. Separate assessor pool
 s cover general arts\, Nga toi Maori and Pacific arts\, and applications a
 re peer-assessed. Deaf and disabled applicants can claim accessibility cos
 ts on top of the grant. Round 2 of 2026 opened 17 August 2026 and closes a
 t 1.00pm NZ time on 17 September 2026\, with results due 2 December 2026. 
 Apply through the Creative New Zealand portal. No application fee.\n\nOrga
 nisation: Creative New Zealand (Arts Council of New Zealand Toi Aotearoa)\
 nLocation: Aotearoa New Zealand. Applicants must be New Zealand citizens o
 r permanent residents. Arts organisations and groups cannot apply to this 
 fund.\nAward: Two tiers: up to NZ$50\,000\, or between NZ$50\,000 and NZ$1
 25\,000. Deaf and disabled applicants can claim additional accessibility c
 osts. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\, across the funded act
 ivity period.\n\nMore: https://creativenz.govt.nz/funding-and-support/all-
 opportunities/creative-impact-fund?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://creativenz.govt.nz/funding-and-support/all-opportunities/creati
 ve-impact-fund?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Aotearoa New Zealand. Applicants must be New Zealand citizens or p
 ermanent residents. Arts organisations and groups cannot apply to this fun
 d.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:creative-nz-international-arts-impact-fund-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T210426Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260921
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260922
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative New Zealand: International Arts Impact Fund 2026
DESCRIPTION:The International Arts Impact Fund is Creative New Zealand's mu
 lti-year fund for established New Zealand artists\, practitioners and arts
  organisations building sustained international careers rather than taking
  a single trip abroad. Up to NZ$75\,000 per year for one\, two or three ca
 lendar years\, so a three-year award can reach NZ$225\,000. ELIGIBILITY: N
 ew Zealand citizens or permanent residents\, and New Zealand-based arts or
 ganisations and groups\, who can show substantial previous international e
 xperience and evidence of international demand for their work. Artists and
  practitioners are prioritised in the 2026 round. PROCESS AND DATES: a two
 -stage application. The expression of interest opened 24 August 2026 and c
 loses at 1.00pm NZ time on 21 September 2026\; those invited through submi
 t a full application by 1.00pm NZ time on 1 October 2026\; results are ann
 ounced 9 December 2026. The EOI is the operative deadline\, so treat 21 Se
 ptember 2026 as the date to hit. Apply through the Creative New Zealand po
 rtal. No application fee.\n\nOrganisation: Creative New Zealand (Arts Coun
 cil of New Zealand Toi Aotearoa)\nLocation: Aotearoa New Zealand\, for sus
 tained international activity. Applicants must be New Zealand citizens or 
 permanent residents\, or New Zealand-based arts organisations and groups.\
 nAward: Up to NZ$75\,000 per year\, for one\, two or three calendar years 
 (so up to NZ$225\,000 over three years). No application fee.\nDuration: On
 e\, two or three calendar years of international activity.\n\nMore: https:
 //creativenz.govt.nz/funding-and-support/all-opportunities/international-a
 rts-impact-fund?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://creativenz.govt.nz/funding-and-support/all-opportunities/intern
 ational-arts-impact-fund?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
LOCATION:Aotearoa New Zealand\, for sustained international activity. Appli
 cants must be New Zealand citizens or permanent residents\, or New Zealand
 -based arts organisations and groups.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:creative-nz-creative-fellowship-fund-2026-round-2@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T210426Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260924
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260925
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative New Zealand: Creative Fellowship Fund 2026 (Roun
 d 2)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Fellowship Fund buys artists and practitioners tim
 e: paid months to develop their practice and make new work\, with no requi
 rement that anything be finished or public at the end. NZ$25\,000 funds up
  to six months\, NZ$50\,000 funds up to twelve\, and the money can go to l
 iving costs\, materials and the resources needed to develop the work. ELIG
 IBILITY: New Zealand citizens or permanent residents\, applying as individ
 uals or as a group of collaborators\; arts organisations cannot apply\, th
 ough sole traders and people operating through a company can apply as indi
 viduals. ASSESSMENT: peer assessors weigh whether the proposal encourages 
 creative risk-taking and new ideas\, supports artistic growth and experime
 ntation\, advances your artistic goals\, and is timely for your career sta
 ge. NZ$50\,000 applications are additionally judged on knowledge-sharing a
 nd what the work does for the artform or community. Separate assessor pool
 s cover general arts\, Nga toi Maori and Pacific arts. No budget is requir
 ed in the application\, and Creative New Zealand explicitly permits AI too
 ls for drafting. Round 2 of 2026 opened 17 August 2026 and closes at 1.00p
 m NZ time on 24 September 2026\, with results due 2 December 2026. Apply t
 hrough the Creative New Zealand portal. No application fee.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Creative New Zealand (Arts Council of New Zealand Toi Aotearoa)\nLocati
 on: Aotearoa New Zealand. Applicants must be New Zealand citizens or perma
 nent residents. Arts organisations cannot apply.\nAward: NZ$25\,000 for up
  to six months of work\, or NZ$50\,000 for up to twelve months. Covers liv
 ing costs\, materials and the resources needed to develop new work. Deaf a
 nd disabled applicants can claim additional accessibility costs. No applic
 ation fee.\nDuration: Up to six months (NZ$25\,000) or up to twelve months
  (NZ$50\,000).\n\nMore: https://creativenz.govt.nz/funding-and-support/all
 -opportunities/creative-fellowship-fund?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://creativenz.govt.nz/funding-and-support/all-opportunities/creati
 ve-fellowship-fund?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
LOCATION:Aotearoa New Zealand. Applicants must be New Zealand citizens or p
 ermanent residents. Arts organisations cannot apply.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:creative-nz-early-career-fund-2026-round-2@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T210426Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative New Zealand: Early Career Fund (Toi Tipu Toi Rea
 ) 2026 Round 2
DESCRIPTION:Toi Tipu Toi Rea\, Creative New Zealand's Early Career Fund\, g
 ives up to NZ$10\,000 to artists and practitioners at the early stage of t
 heir career to create work\, pick up new skills\, pay a mentor and share w
 hat they make with their communities. No professional track record is requ
 ired\, which makes it one of the few substantial public grants open to peo
 ple who have not built a CV yet. ELIGIBILITY: New Zealand citizens or perm
 anent residents who are early in their career\, applying as individuals or
  as a collaborative group. Established artists\, arts organisations and gr
 oups cannot apply. PROCESS: no budget is needed up front\; applicants answ
 er four reflective questions about their artistic goals and supply support
 ing material such as an artistic CV or work samples. AI tools are permitte
 d for drafting and refining the application. Peer assessors judge whether 
 the activity fosters artistic growth at a critical career stage\, with fin
 al decisions made by Creative New Zealand's Head of Investment. Round 2 of
  2026 opened 31 August 2026 and closes at 1.00pm NZ time on 1 October 2026
 \; results are announced 9 December 2026\, and funded activity must take p
 lace between 9 December 2026 and 31 December 2027. Apply through the Creat
 ive New Zealand portal. No application fee.\n\nOrganisation: Creative New 
 Zealand (Arts Council of New Zealand Toi Aotearoa)\nLocation: Aotearoa New
  Zealand. Applicants must be New Zealand citizens or permanent residents a
 t an early stage of their career. Established artists\, organisations and 
 groups cannot apply.\nAward: Up to NZ$10\,000. Covers making work\, gainin
 g new skills and paying mentors. Deaf and disabled applicants can claim ad
 ditional accessibility costs. No application fee.\nDuration: Activity must
  take place between 9 December 2026 and 31 December 2027.\n\nMore: https:/
 /creativenz.govt.nz/funding-and-support/all-opportunities/early-career-fun
 d---toi-tipu-toi-rea?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refe
 rral
URL:https://creativenz.govt.nz/funding-and-support/all-opportunities/early-
 career-fund---toi-tipu-toi-rea?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
LOCATION:Aotearoa New Zealand. Applicants must be New Zealand citizens or p
 ermanent residents at an early stage of their career. Established artists\
 , organisations and groups cannot apply.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:creative-australia-arts-projects-organisations-2026@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T210426Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative Australia: Arts Projects for Organisations (Sept
 ember 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Creative Australia's principal open-round project grant for art
 s organisations and the most directly relevant Australian scheme for mount
 ing festivals\, exhibitions and public programmes. The guidelines explicit
 ly list festivals\, productions\, exhibitions\, performances\, touring\, p
 ublishing\, recording\, collaborations\, research and community engagement
  as supported activity. Organisations may propose either a single project 
 or an entire programme of projects\, which can extend to a full artistic p
 rogramme for a given calendar year or longer\, so this can function as de 
 facto annual programme funding. The category is artform-agnostic and routi
 nely supports media arts\, digital culture\, experimental sound and art-an
 d-science work\; activity delivered online is explicitly permitted. NOTABL
 E: international organisations are eligible where the project demonstrably
  benefits practising Australian artists\, their work\, or Australian audie
 nces\, so a non-Australian festival can apply if it is programming Austral
 ian artists. The applicant must be a legally constituted entity: incorpora
 ted association\, company limited by guarantee\, or government statutory a
 uthority. Registration in the Application Management System must be comple
 ted at least one business day before the closing date. The round closes 1 
 September 2026 at 3pm AEST.\n\nOrganisation: Creative Australia\nLocation:
  Activity may take place nationally within Australia\, internationally\, o
 r online.\nAward: AUD 20\,000 to 100\,000. No matching or co-financing req
 uirement. No application fee. Organisational administrative costs should g
 enerally not exceed 10 percent of the total project budget or the applicat
 ion becomes less competitive.\nDuration: Activity must last no longer than
  two years from the proposed start date\; the project must commence after 
 notification and within one year of it.\n\nMore: https://creative.gov.au/i
 nvestments-opportunities/arts-projects-organisations?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://creative.gov.au/investments-opportunities/arts-projects-organis
 ations?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activity may take place nationally within Australia\, internationa
 lly\, or online.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:creative-australia-international-engagement-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T210426Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261014
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative Australia: International Engagement Fund (Octobe
 r 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Supports reciprocal international exchange between Australian p
 ractitioners or organisations and confirmed overseas partners\, which make
 s it the right instrument for co-hosted convenings\, labs and cross-border
  programme partnerships rather than one-way touring. Supported activity ty
 pes are creative collaboration and development\, cultural exchange and kno
 wledge sharing\, and labs and practice-exchange models\, mapping closely o
 nto media arts residencies\, art-and-science research exchanges and digita
 l culture symposia. Eligible costs include artist fees\, travel\, accommod
 ation\, production expenses\, marketing\, access costs\, and childcare or 
 carer support. International organisations are eligible where the project 
 benefits Australian artists or creative workers\, and a confirmed internat
 ional partner is mandatory and must confirm participation in writing. The 
 reciprocity requirement is substantive: the strongest applications embed m
 utually beneficial exchange rather than simply presenting an Australian ar
 tist abroad. Creative Australia's published assessment feedback notes top-
 ranked applications foregrounded First Nations self-determined or diaspori
 c-led activity and demonstrated sector-wide impact. It is competitive: 157
  eligible applications in the March 2026 round yielded 33 grants\, about a
  21 percent success rate. Contemporary music practitioners are excluded an
 d directed to Music Australia programmes. Closes 13 October 2026 at 3pm AE
 DT. WHO CAN APPLY: 'individuals\, groups and organisations (including smal
 l businesses) may apply to this category.' Individual applicants must be a
 n Australian citizen or permanent resident. A legally constituted entity i
 s not required\, so unincorporated groups are eligible.\n\nOrganisation: C
 reative Australia\nLocation: International\, with a confirmed overseas par
 tner.\nAward: AUD 5\,000 to 30\,000. No application fee. No formal matchin
 g requirement\, but assessment explicitly weighs diversity and scale of in
 come and co-funding\, including earned income\, grants\, sponsorship and i
 n-kind contributions.\nDuration: Activities must not exceed two years from
  the proposed start date\; supported activity must fall between 1 July 202
 6 and 1 July 2028.\n\nMore: https://creative.gov.au/investments-opportunit
 ies/international-engagement-fund?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
URL:https://creative.gov.au/investments-opportunities/international-engagem
 ent-fund?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:International\, with a confirmed overseas partner.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:copyright-agency-non-fiction-writing-fellowship-2026@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T210426Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260817
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260818
SUMMARY:Deadline: Copyright Agency Cultural Fund: Fellowship for Non-Fictio
 n Writing 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Copyright Agency Cultural Fund's Fellowship for Non-Fiction
  Writing awards AUD 80\,000 to one mid-career or established Australian au
 thor to research and write a substantial new work of literary non-fiction.
  Eligible forms include memoir\, biography\, history\, criticism\, arts an
 d science writing\, and environmental and political writing. ELIGIBILITY: 
 mid-career or established Australian authors with a demonstrated publicati
 on record and publisher interest in the proposed work\; Australian residen
 ts only. APPLICATIONS open 20 April 2026 and close 17 August 2026\, 1:00pm
  AEST. Apply via the Cultural Fund fellowship page.\n\nOrganisation: Copyr
 ight Agency (Cultural Fund)\nLocation: Australia\; Australian authors only
 .\nAward: AUD 80\,000 (one fellowship). No application fee.\nDuration: Fel
 lowship to research and write a new work\n\nMore: https://www.copyright.co
 m.au/culturalfund/fellowship/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
URL:https://www.copyright.com.au/culturalfund/fellowship/?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Australia\; Australian authors only.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:copyright-agency-author-fellowship-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260904T210426Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260817
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260818
SUMMARY:Deadline: Copyright Agency Cultural Fund: Author Fellowship 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Copyright Agency Cultural Fund's Author Fellowship awards A
 UD 80\,000 to one established Australian author to create a significant ne
 w work for publication. ELIGIBILITY: established Australian authors with c
 ritical acclaim and confirmed publisher interest in the proposed work\; Au
 stralian residents only. This is a separate fellowship from the Cultural F
 und's Fellowship for Non-Fiction Writing\, though administered on the same
  cycle. APPLICATIONS close 17 August 2026\, 1:00pm AEST. Apply via the Cul
 tural Fund fellowship page.\n\nOrganisation: Copyright Agency (Cultural Fu
 nd)\nLocation: Australia\; Australian authors only.\nAward: AUD 80\,000 (o
 ne fellowship). No application fee.\nDuration: Fellowship to create a new 
 work\n\nMore: https://www.copyright.com.au/culturalfund/fellowship/?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.copyright.com.au/culturalfund/fellowship/?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Australia\; Australian authors only.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:blackbird-foundation-believers-fund-iii-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260904T210426Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270630
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270701
SUMMARY:Deadline: Blackbird Foundation: Believers Fund III 2026
DESCRIPTION:Believers funds the people\, projects and programs creating the
  conditions for young people's creativity to flourish at scale. Creativity
  is meant in the broadest sense: artists are creative\, but so are scienti
 sts\, debaters\, community builders and dancers\, and a project can be any
 thing from a summer camp to a robotics competition to a co-working holiday
  house for artists. Blackbird looks for inventive\, dynamic experiments th
 at encourage young people to be curious\, to explore\, to be lifelong lear
 ners\, and to build community and become high-agency people\, backing proj
 ects that are 0-1 (just starting) or 1-10 (scaling or iterating) rather th
 an established groups. Examples: a neighbourhood community science lab\, a
  hacker house\, a hardware garage makerspace\, a travelling STEM roadshow\
 , or an after-school arts or coding club. ELIGIBILITY (no flexibility): in
 dividuals\, groups or organisations established in Australia and/or New Ze
 aland\; projects taking place in AU/NZ\; projects completed within 12 mont
 hs\; projects whose core focus is primarily creative outcomes\; and organi
 sations with less than AUD 1.5M in revenue. WHEN TO APPLY: Believers is op
 en year-round\, with EOIs and applications reviewed and progressed on a ro
 lling basis\; the program closes when all funds are disbursed or at the en
 d of the FY27 period (30 June 2027)\, whichever comes first. Expressions o
 f interest for Believers Fund III open on 30 June 2026.\n\nOrganisation: B
 lackbird Foundation\nLocation: Australia and/or New Zealand\; individuals\
 , groups or organisations established in AU/NZ\, with projects taking plac
 e in AU/NZ.\nAward: AUD 5\,000 and AUD 10\,000 grants. No application fee.
 \nDuration: Projects must be completed within 12 months\n\nMore: https://w
 ww.blackbird.foundation/projects?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
URL:https://www.blackbird.foundation/projects?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Australia and/or New Zealand\; individuals\, groups or organisatio
 ns established in AU/NZ\, with projects taking place in AU/NZ.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
